<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Event Sourcing on Jens Rantil</title><link>https://jensrantil.github.io/tags/event-sourcing/</link><description>Recent content in Event Sourcing on Jens Rantil</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 10 Jan 2025 13:33:12 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jensrantil.github.io/tags/event-sourcing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>CQRS+Event Sourcing Messaging Patterns</title><link>https://jensrantil.github.io/posts/cqrs-event-sourcing-messaging-patterns/</link><pubDate>Sun, 26 May 2013 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jensrantil.github.io/posts/cqrs-event-sourcing-messaging-patterns/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This post is partially related to my &lt;a href="%7cfilename%7cCQRS-time-to-rewind.rst" &gt;previous blog&#10;post&lt;/a&gt; about&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.github.com/JensRantil/rewind" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Rewind&lt;/a&gt; and&#10;&lt;a href="http://www.github.com/JensRantil/gorewind" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Gorewind&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Designing a decoupled, message based, system based on the&#10;&lt;a href="http://martinfowler.com/bliki/CQRS.html" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;CQRS&lt;/a&gt; pattern together with&#10;&lt;a href="http://martinfowler.com/eaaDev/EventSourcing.html" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;event sourcing&lt;/a&gt;&#10;require some thought. Since I&amp;rsquo;ve been thinking about it for a while now,&#10;I thought I&amp;rsquo;d share some thoughts so far.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="cqrs"&gt;&#10; CQRS&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#cqrs"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;First let&amp;rsquo;s think about the way information conceptually flows in a CQRS&#10;system:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Client issuing a command -&amp;gt; Command -&amp;gt; Command Handler -&amp;gt;&#10;Event -&amp;gt; Event Listeners/Projections&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>